## Why This Is Asked
This question simulates a live order book and tests dynamic range sums alongside top-k queries within a price band. It combines segment trees with per-node order statistics and requires careful handling of cancellations to maintain consistent state.

## Key Concepts
- **Dynamic segment tree** over the price domain for efficient range queries
- **Per-node multisets** to support kthLargest queries with duplicate prices
- **Order ID mapping** (idMap) for O(1) updates and cancellations
- **Amortized O(log² n)** operations: O(log n) tree traversal × O(log n) multiset operations

## Memory Handling
The idMap stores each active order's metadata, enabling O(1) lookups for updates and cancellations. When an order is cancelled, its entry is removed from both the idMap and the relevant multiset, ensuring no memory leaks. The segment tree nodes are created lazily on demand, only when prices are actually inserted.

## Cancellations
Cancellations require removing a specific quantity from a price node's multiset—O(log n) for the multiset operation plus O(log n) for updating the segment tree. This maintains accurate totals for both sum and kthLargest queries.

## Code Example
```javascript
class DynamicOrderBook {
  constructor() {
    this.idMap = new Map();
    this.segmentTree = null;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a dynamic string structure supporting weighted, prefix-based queries and order-statistics. A Trie augmented with per-node aggregates enables efficient prefix sums and k-th retrieval while handling duplicates via cumulative weights.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node aggregates (subtreeWeight, terminalWeight)
- O(len(word)) time complexity for insert/erase operations
- O(len(prefix)) for prefix-sum queries
- O(len(prefix) + len(target_word)) for kth-word queries
- Duplicate handling via cumulative weight values

## Code Example
```javascript
class WeightedTrie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }

  insertWord(word, w) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      const idx = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[idx]) node.children[idx] = new TrieNode();
      node = node.children[idx];
      node.subtreeWeight += w;
    }
    node.terminalWeight += w;
  }

  eraseWord(word, w) {
    this.insertWord(word, -w);
  }

  queryPrefixSum(prefix) {
    let node = this.traverse(prefix);
    return node ? node.subtreeWeight : 0;
  }

  kthWordWithPrefix(prefix, k) {
    let node = this.traverse(prefix);
    if (!node || node.subtreeWeight < k) return null;
    let word = prefix;
    while (!node.terminalWeight) {
      for (let i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
        if (!node.children[i]) continue;
        if (node.children[i].subtreeWeight >= k) {
          word += String.fromCharCode(97 + i);
          node = node.children[i];
          break;
        }
        k -= node.children[i].subtreeWeight;
      }
    }
    return word;
  }

  traverse(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      const idx = char.charCodeAt(0) - 97;
      if (!node.children[idx]) return null;
      node = node.children[idx];
    }
    return node;
  }
}

class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Array(26).fill(null);
    this.subtreeWeight = 0;
    this.terminalWeight = 0;
  }
}
```

